WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.680
In a perfect world, every awesome video game
idea would become a reality…but our world

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.059
isn't perfect, and many sure-fire hit games
never make it past the beta stage.

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:16.760
It's a shame to lose out on the copious amounts
of sheer fun many of these games would've

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.760
generated.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.030
So, let's sift through the scrapyard of canceled
games and pick out some buried treasures.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.030
"Woah!

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.030
Nice graphics!

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.310
I'd like to get my hands on that game!"

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:27.080
Gotham by Gaslight

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.990
Batman plus anything usually equals success.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.720
Well… almost anything.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.370
Based on the comic book of the same name,
Gotham by Gaslight would've been no different.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.239
Players took control of Steampunk Batman,
roaming Victorian England in search of Jack

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.239
the Ripper.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:41.239
Why Jack?

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:44.030
Because after dealing with the Joker for so
long, it's sometimes good to relax with an

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.070
easier foe.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.809
Sadly, Day One Studios, the company behind
Gotham by Gaslight, was unable to sell publisher

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:53.829
THQ on a free-roaming Batman game where Bruce
goes toe-to-toe with one of the most infamous

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:55.120
killers in history.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.969
Gaslight Batman lives on in Lego Batman 3:
Beyond Gotham, Arkham Origins, and Infinite

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.111
Crisis, among others, all of which let you
play as the Victorian-era Dark Knight to your

00:01:03.111 --> 00:01:04.900
heart's desire.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.420
Highlander

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.480
Games based on TV shows and movies are hit-or-miss,
to say the least, but Highlander looked like

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.620
it would've been a hit.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:15.030
Your exploits as an Immortal would've sent
you throughout history to locales like Ancient

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.250
Rome, Pompeii, and New York City…

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.510
Kind of like playing all of the Assassin's
Creed games at once, minus the crappy sequels.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:25.930
You'd also get to perform all sorts of cool
death-defying stunts, like leaping down skyscrapers

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:28.229
or electrocuting yourself, without actually
dying.

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:32.100
They even had an actual writer from the Highlander
TV series to write the project.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.479
Sadly, Square Enix themselves did the butchering,
cancelling the game in 2010 for unknown reasons.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:39.840
The studio was probably too busy dragging
its feet with the next Final Fantasy or Kingdom

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.509
Hearts to set aside a weekend and just finish
Highlander already.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:45.259
Hi-Ten Bomberman

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:49.650
If you enjoy mindless party games as much
as you love fiery explosions, Hi-Ten Bomberman

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.710
would have been your jam.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.149
It was going to be regular Bomberman on steroids,
allowing up to 10 people to play at once.

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:58.600
Either against each other, in groups, or—if
anyone's feeling particularly sadistic—nine

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.939
vs. one.

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:04.070
More Bombers, more bombs, and more explosions—who
could ask for anything more?

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.509
Unfortunately, Hi-Ten Bomberman never went
anywhere, aside from a few Japanese video

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:09.090
game conventions in 1993.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:13.160
Now that we have ultra-HD and online multiplayer,
why not give it another go?

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.460
In a society that still actively enjoys turning
each other into crispy critters, Hi-Ten Bomberman

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.870
would be a smash hit today.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.290
B.C.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.550
In Intrepid Computer Entertainment's B.C.,
you control a tribe of Neanderthals on a quest

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:29.570
to kill anyone not in your tribe, thereby
evolving the human race in your image.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:33.350
Along the way, you have to battle angry apes
and gigantic, man-eating dinosaurs, both of

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.390
whom hate everything about you except your
rich, meaty flavor.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.030
Sadly, B.C. was simply too ambitious.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:42.870
Planned features included changing weather,
an epic food chain, independently functioning

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.780
NPCs, and the ability to choose who to let
into your tribe.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.920
The project was cancelled in 2004, but in
the modern gaming scene, B.C. would fit right

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.160
in, and likely be among the best.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.310
Insane

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.590
Lots of us love survival horror games, so
imagine somebody who truly knows horror giving

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:58.730
it a shot.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.650
This would have been the case with Insane,
a 2012 game directed by Guillermo del Toro

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.800
of Hellboy and Pan's Labyrinth fame.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.780
Insane was to be the most terrifying sandbox
game of all time.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.620
Plus, del Toro had an entire trilogy in mind.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.900
Financial difficulties forced THQ to focus
solely on guaranteed hits, however, rather

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.880
than experimental horror projects.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.700
Currently, del Toro owns all the rights to
Insane, so he could always make it a reality

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.590
with another game company, or simply turn
it into a badass movie franchise…

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:28.630
Provided he's not too busy explaining why
Hellboy 3 still isn't happening.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.840
Silent Hills

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.870
Another abandoned Guillermo del Toro project,
Silent Hills was supposed to be the director’s

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.840
collaboration with Metal Gear series creator
Hideo Kojima.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.230
Add The Walking Dead’s Norman Reedus and
you have a guaranteed win.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:43.580
This trifecta of legendary figures would have
made for an incredible psychological horror

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.760
experience on the PS4, but it was sadly canceled.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.380
Rumors had it that Kojima was leaving Konami,
which was why the project was pulled.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.870
P.T., the playable teaser for the game, was
pulled from the PlayStation Store as well,

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:57.070
but you can still relive the terror if you
kept the demo in your library.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.480
Sadly, it's the closest you'll ever get to
Silent Hills.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.540
Star Wars 1313

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.790
As a young Boba Fett, Star Wars 1313 would
allow you to navigate the wretched hive of

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.410
scum and villainy that is the underground
Coruscant, where there are no Jedi to keep

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.420
the peace.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:15.870
1313 focused almost entirely on guns, blasters,
and whatever else a bounty hunter would need

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.400
to get his dirty job done.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.310
Unfortunately, this amazing concept couldn't
survive the one thing more evil than the Dark

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.410
Side: corporate takeovers.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.220
When Disney bought the Star Wars franchise
in 2012, it cancelled anything LucasArts had

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.300
in the pipeline, including 1313.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.720
Current Star Wars game publisher, EA, has
shown little interest in 1313, preferring

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.780
to focus on more mainstream, canonical games
like Battlefront.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.910
LucasArts, meanwhile... has given us Angry
Birds Star Wars II.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:46.630
Star Wars 1313 is left somewhere in the junkyard,
likely near Luke Skywalker's dismembered hand.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.320
Mega Man Universe

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.480
Mega Man is awesome.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.430
That’s pretty much just science.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.090
Know what would have been even more awesome?

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.810
The ability to make your own levels and customize
your very own Mega Man.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.210
Just think Mario Maker.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.560
That was the premise for Mega Man Universe,
a side-scrolling platformer that was supposed

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.230
to be released on Xbox Live Arcade and the
PlayStation Network.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:08.160
We would have loved to have seen what kind
of sick, twisted platforming gauntlets creative

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.250
players could have shared online if this game
came to fruition.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.760
And even cooler was the fact that Ryu from
Street Fighter and Arthur from Ghosts 'n Goblins

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.590
were planned as DLC characters.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.750
Sadly, the game was cancelled in 2011, so
now we only have our super fighting robot

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.070
dreams to hang onto.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.250
Star Fox 2

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.250
Releasing a direct sequel to the original
Star Fox on the Super Nintendo would have

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.910
been a no-brainer, but it didn't work out
that way.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.950
Star Fox 2 would have continued the story
and reassembled the original team to fight

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:38.620
Emperor Andross and protect the Lylat system,
including new ships and new characters.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.190
Unfortunately, the arrival of the Nintendo
64 stopped development on the title, although

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.390
Japanese versions of the prototype leaked
online in 2015.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.400
It might not have seen the light of day as
an official Super Nintendo game, but Star

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.960
Fox 2 is alive out there somewhere, and we'd
still love to barrel roll through it.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.270
Thanks for watching!

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.070
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:58.940
And leave us a comment to let us know which
lost games you’d like to play...

